{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Now, however, also about our journey; — I wrote to you from Brussels, — in this letter you will find when we departed, — I believe it was Monday, after we had previously in the evening watched the illumination in the city on the occasion of the Queen’s first appearance — the sister of our King!) — So first via Leuven to Liège — a rich country — the next day to Aachen — saw the Cathedral with lights and [we] sat again on Emperor Charles’s throne, then to Cologne — both short day’s journeys — from Liège to Aachen, especially beautiful and rich countryside, — in Liège as in Leuven and Ghent beautiful university buildings; we looked around at these universities, as a future place of rest, if the priests in Berlin finally drive me out of the Copper Ditch entirely; the Curia in Rome would in any case be a more honorable opponent, than the wretchedness of a wretched priestly rabble in Berlin). So arrived in Cologne on Wednesday afternoon, immediately collected your dear letter, — thereby learned that the express mail only reaches Cassel on Friday, i.e. today, — then still in Cologne, — instead of vegetating in this old, ugly city among curiosities on Thursday, made a detour to Bonn, the dear, old friend Windischmann on my part — and then jointly Mr. v. Schlegel“) — first his house by force — and when he had finally come out of it — visited him with all cordiality and cheerfulness — however, the good or rather most stately — and comfortable arrangement of the house — except for the chicken yard and the peacock perch and their painting and arrangement — I reserve for the oral description; only of a woman, whom one might look for there, there is nothing to mention; yet one does not miss her entirely, for if not female, then something feminine is perhaps already found there. — We could indeed have spent several days pleasantly and seriously (though we are generally not inclined to do so) and interestingly in Bonn. That we spent this morning usefully with another visit to the sublime Cathedral, the Wallraf collection, inspection of the dying Marie etc., eating oysters, drinking Mosel wine etc., — must conclude with the addition, that I then alone arrived here at noon with a second crossing of the Wupper in the company of some student tobacco pipes."}}],"created":1795220961,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":495,"prompt_tokens":674,"total_tokens":1169,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-ShKIB8ysJxIAf0zt8fM4GoT0qgjtpTMz","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":674,"prompt_ms":759.103,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.1262655786350149,"prompt_per_second":887.8900491764623,"predicted_n":495,"predicted_ms":11549.225,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.378997975708504,"predicted_per_second":42.773432849390325}}